                <pb facs="0832" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg818"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morrill, United States commissioner, to Mr. Hoar,
                        Attorney-General</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Macon, Georgia</hi></placeName>,
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-09-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >September</hi> 6, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Attorney-General United
                        States</hi>:</p>
                <p>Colonel Milledge, with Deputy Marshals Watson and Cox with <hi
                        rendition="#italic">posse comitatus</hi>, left for Fort Gaines this morning.
                    Report that filibusters could not get over shoals in river.</p>
                <p><seg type="margin">[116]</seg> *Have forwarded your telegrams.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. C. MORRILL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States
                            Commissioner.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
